      "message": "[error] Line 304: 🔴 Catching `std::exception` and then returning success now swallows unexpected sync-processing failures as if the frame was handled. That can silently drop state updates while keeping the stream alive, masking protocol/data corruption and making convergence/debugging much harder. Keep recoverable metadata errors local (already done in `onSyncData`), but for this generic catch return an error (as before) so the sync channel is reset on unexpected exceptions.",
